questions.stem:
A turnstile tester sums a comma pair with this fragment:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("12,34");
sc.useDelimiter(",");
int t = sc.nextInt() + sc.nextInt();
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?

A kiosk expects commas but receives semicolons, then crashes here:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("7;9");
sc.useDelimiter(",");
int a = sc.nextInt();
What is the fault?

A coach splits one results row with this fragment:
String line = "mia,82";
Scanner row = new Scanner(line);
row.useDelimiter(_____);
Which argument belongs in the blank?

A donation jar totals spaced coins with this fragment:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("  8   15  ");
int t = 0;
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { t += sc.nextInt(); }
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?

A timing crew sums a semicolon row with this fragment:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("4;11;6");
sc.useDelimiter(";");
int t = 0;
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { t += sc.nextInt(); }
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?

A nursery counts planted rows while ignoring blanks:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("elm\n\noak\n\npine");
int n = 0;
while (sc.hasNextLine()) { if (!sc.nextLine().trim().isEmpty()) n++; }
System.out.println(n);
What integer is printed?

A market guard skips short rows before indexing:
String[] parts = line.split(",");
if (_____) continue;
int qty = Integer.parseInt(parts[1].trim());
Which test belongs in the blank?

A rainfall import crashes on the row west,N/A here:
int mm = Integer.parseInt(parts[1]);
What is the fault?

A dock scanner tracks the lightest crate with this fragment:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("18 25 11 29 16");
int best = sc.nextInt();
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { int v = sc.nextInt(); if (v < best) best = v; }
System.out.println(best);
What integer is printed?

Before dawn a produce report opens with a title row that the totals must ignore:
Scanner sc = new Scanner(new File("sales.csv"));
_____;
while (sc.hasNextLine()) { String line = sc.nextLine(); }
Which line belongs in the blank?

On a rainy platform a fare box mixes coins with a stray word in this fragment:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("5 skip 15 25");
int t = 0;
while (sc.hasNext()) { if (sc.hasNextInt()) t += sc.nextInt(); else sc.next(); }
System.out.println(t);
What integer is printed?

A quiz desk counts strong scores in this stream:
Scanner sc = new Scanner("61 48 77 55 82");
int n = 0;
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { if (sc.nextInt() >= 60) n++; }
System.out.println(n);
What integer is printed?

Under stadium lights, an analyst averages lap counts streaming from a file:
int sum = 0, n = 0;
while (sc.hasNextInt()) { sum += sc.nextInt(); n++; }
double avg = _____;
Which expression belongs in the blank?

A timing page shows 3.0 instead of 3.5 because of this line:
double avg = sum / n;
Here sum holds 7 and n holds 2. What is the fault?
